{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice","id":1554478,"title":"Would you leave this world for a D&D world if given the choice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-19T11:06:26-07:00","id":1554478,"title":"Would you leave this world for a D&D world if given the choice?","content":"If you could leave this world to live in a D&amp;D (or pathfinder) world, would you do it and why?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In my case; I absolutely would since ALL D&amp;D worlds, even the really hostile and shitty ones like Dark Sun have a factor this world does not; linear progression. Any commoner who has the simple gumption to do so, can better their lot in life by leaving the quotidian script society applies to their lives and venturing out into the unknown to find their fortune. The instant you start doing this, you start earning EXP (unless your DM is one of those milestone people), and you start seeing measurable improvement in yourself and you life. It sounds ridiculous until you realize that D&amp;D worlds are lousy with buried ruins, lost keeps, monster lairs, and all manner of magicked insanity waiting to be discovered. A simple snatch and grab can set you up for a year, and a large enough score is a total quality of life upgrade.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here in our world you can work your ass off your entire life just like the aforementioned commoner, but if you step one foot out of society\u2019s script you\u2019ll face everything from social shunning to jail time. Barriers to your success will materialize like magic to make sure you stay mired in whatever social stratum the bastards in control arbitrarily placed you in. And despite claims of meritocracy, no amount of work will ever make a difference since it\u2019s all about social standing and clout. Yes in D&amp;D there\u2019s things like bandits/brigands/pirates/thieves, but those already exist here in our world and have existed for all of time. Yes D&amp;D worlds have plagues and such, but we just got out of a pandemic without any clerical healing to work with. There\u2019s entitled and self-absorbed nobles and a feudalistic system, but what do you think the billionaires are trying to do with this country now? There\u2019s monsters that can raid smaller settlements and infest cities, but weigh that against hate-groups, psychos, and gestapos running amok.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T11:44:21-07:00","id":1554483,"title":"","content":"I understand your frustration, but it wouldn't work out as well as you think.<br /> <br /> You're assuming everyone follows PC rules in D&amp;D settings to begin with, but that's not the case.<br /> <br /> Most people in the setting don't get XP or follow level progression rules (level progression is universal only in 3rd edition, but even there XP isn't). Adventurers are exceptional people even at level 1. They get better stats, better abilities, better HP rules, better equipment, better everything.<br /> <br /> General society in D&amp;D isn't all that far from the shitty situation in our world. Most people don't have regular access to Clerics and spells in general, at least not in a way they can control. Living as an adventurer, even if available to you, is hardship after hardship and most of your money going to things that may be beautiful, but aren't there for your comfort, but for your survival.<br /> <br /> Working under the conditions we do IRL is hard for a long list of reasons, and meritocracy is an offensive joke. But have you ever actually went hungry or faced physical danger? I did, and even being just a fraction of what D&amp;D characters (or a lot of real people, actually) go through, I don't want to be there again.<br /> <br /> That's actually what makes the people in power so powerful, and lock us in shitty jobs: this is far from the situation our society could and should afford us, but is still far better than the alternative, even a fantasy alternative.<br /> <br /> Don't waste your time and energy wishing to live in a escapist fantasy. Use the escapist fantasy to help you cope, but otherwise take this anger and turn it into political action, as small as it may be, to improve your life. It's also a frustrating path, but the only one that can really pay up to any degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T09:20:08-07:00","id":1554555,"title":"","content":"Lovely, that's more or less what I've been hearing out of people from all directions for the last ten, twenty, hell going on thirty years now. You even included the classic &quot;someone, somewhere has it worse&quot; argument that never actually solved anything. Every time something does become incrementally better, even after all our effort is directed towards it, it immediately falls flat on its face and gets even worse in the next term. It's almost like the entire system is structured to make such advances pointless isn't it? Promising change in the future when it never occurs in my lifetime doesn't help, its just more empty words. So hope doesn't pan out, work doesn't matter, we can't even escape apparently, so what exactly would you have me do then? Is there a point at which people finally realize that faith which is never rewarded is synonymous with being scammed or is the human race truly that deluded?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T12:52:32-07:00","id":1554561,"title":"","content":"You didn't ask if there are fictional worlds people would rather live in, you cited as specific style of fictional world and someone responded with very clear reasons why it's not actually better to live under those conditions.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of examples of fictional worlds where, yeah, I'd love to escape to them if that was somehow a possibility. This world does, in fact, suck. But D&amp;D style fantasy worlds? Fuck no. I know this is a controversial piece of fiction, but if you want to understand why... go read/watch Goblin Slayer because part of the core themes of the show is that D&amp;D style fantasy worlds are inherently screwed up in horrific ways. When your fate is ruled by dice, eventually the gods roll badly on your behalf... and unlike a player of a TTRPG you're going to experience it all for real.<br /> <br /> Someone wants to send me to the core worlds in Lancer? Cool. I'd love to be part of a post-scarcity near-utopia where the vast majority of humanity lives comfortable lives free to pursue their intellectual desires without worrying about jobs just to get by. People that want to change the cosmos in a grand fashion can go join the Auxiliaries if they want danger and excitement, but the rest of us get to be safe and sound doing whatever we find productive for society in our own ways and follow our motivations as we see best. A universe where the government isn't perfect, but is honestly trying its best to balance its vast population with a democratic system that could (and has in the past) voted in tyrannical governments as the most pressing political issue and is doing a decent job? Yeah, sounds good.<br /> <br /> Of course, since we can't just all hop in a portal and get zapped over to that, nor are trucks actually blessed with the power to yeet us into other dimensions... we're stuck here in reality and have to real with it. Part of reality is that real lasting change? It's slow. The idea that history is defined by these singular moments (or worse people) were special things happen and blam... everything changes? That's the scam. Real change is slow. It's frustrating hard work. It can take decades, even centuries, to actually get humans to change on a mass scale that's no longer going to be at serious risk of backsliding. Your grandchildren might die of old age before the fight you care about finally bares fruit. But it's never going to happen if nobody ever starts.<br /> <br /> There's an interesting bit of folklore where it seems like pretty much every agrarian civilization has it's own version of a &quot;Rip Van Winkle&quot; style story. As far as most academics conclude, these are not related as if some myth got passed around, but an independent phenomenon as it serves a distinct purpose for orienting early agrarian cultures towards long term social thinking. Building a successful agrarian society takes time. It takes generations to cultivate land until it can fully sustain the people you have, let a lone expand the population. People need to develop strategies that encourage activities meant to benefit later generations: good water infrastructure, planting long gestation crops, communal mills or presses, etc. So stories about men falling asleep only to wake up and see how far things have come along seem to be common because it says that yes, eventually, the hard work will pay off even if not for you.<br /> <br /> Modern highly technological societies (like anyone posting here probably lives in) reach a point where those stories get a bit lost because technology lets us build things up so much faster. We don't have to wait decades for certain cash crops to finally become profitable but if maintained will be profitable for generations forward. We have, in many ways, lost touch with that mindset and thus with a fundamental aspect of what makes civilization function. Our world isn't going to get better if we accept sorrow that what we build today isn't going to make our lives better at the cost of the joy of building good things for the future we never see ourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T15:52:12-07:00","id":1554567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice?p=1554555#post1554555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovely</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> Adding to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Heavy Arms</a> said, there's not much we can really answer to your questions, either the title or the underlying ones.<br /> <br /> Your frustration is laser-focused on the myth of meritocracy, and then you jump to a setting where meritocracy seems to objectively work.<br /> <br /> But this setting doesn't really have such a straight meritocratic bent, and your very question misses the point that meritocracy isn't the only problem, and the proposed setting has a lot of the other problems hugely augmented.<br /> <br /> We can't say much more without not only being extremely political, but also being <i>specifically</i> political, which is something that'll just prompt a pointless fight in this thread outside very specific circumstances. I can say for sure that meritocracy is a scam to begin with, and that even if D&amp;D really get you actual meritocracy it would still suck. But beyond that anything we have to say will be biased and context-based.<br /> <br /> More to the point: reality sucks, royally, and is frustratingly hard and slow to change. But giving up isn't really an option and change does occur with time, if not in the scale we want. Escapism is a good exercise, but as far as it goes you're getting a lot of things wrong with D&amp;D, and while that isn't a problem in itself (since D&amp;D worlds don't exist for real), it's a problem in how it demonstrates your perception of the real problems and your expectations for their solutions, or how desperate you are for such solutions.<br /> <br /> I'm stuck in a crappy work where my needed adaptations are being revoked and I'll probably have to sue the company. I'm badly paid and my prospects at ever getting a promotion will go from practically zero to absolute zero. So I more or less know how bad it is. I've been fooled by the promise of meritocratic reward for years. I've seen the problems with the system for decades, too. And I do want to give up sometimes. I can't really give you the hope you want in the way you want, I can only say it isn't in taking D&amp;D as a model world to live in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T13:09:11-07:00","id":1554602,"title":"","content":"Just to chime in real quick.. if you get the chance to see The Gamers 4: Dorkness Falls, it goes right along with this thread. I watched the workprint recently, and then seeing this thread reminded me of it!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> At the end of The Gamers: Hands of Fate, the players are seemly trapped in the game world, and the new movie Dorkness Falls deals with the aftermath of that. And brings up some questions about if you'd rather stay there or not...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, if you haven't seen The Gamers movies, I recommend em! You can watch them alll for free on thier website: <a href=\"https://www.zombieorpheus.com/the-gamers/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.zombieorpheus.com/the-gamers/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T14:50:39-07:00","id":1554605,"title":"","content":"Personally I would never go into a D&amp;D world as I like my creature comforts of electricty, indoor plumbing and having better oppturnities in life to much. If there was any places I would go to would be some of the more peaceful planets of Pact Worlds of the StarFinder setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T14:38:16-08:00","id":1557382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice#post1554478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you could leave this world to live in a D&amp;D (or pathfinder) world, would you do it and why?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In my case; I absolutely would since ALL D&amp;D worlds, even the really hostile and shitty ones like Dark Sun have a factor this world does not; linear progression. Any commoner who has the simple gumption to do so, can better their lot in life by leaving the quotidian script society applies to their lives and venturing out into the unknown to find their fortune. The instant you start doing this, you start earning EXP (unless your DM is one of those milestone people), and you start seeing measurable improvement in yourself and you life. It sounds ridiculous until you realize that D&amp;D worlds are lousy with buried ruins, lost keeps, monster lairs, and all manner of magicked insanity waiting to be discovered. A simple snatch and grab can set you up for a year, and a large enough score is a total quality of life upgrade.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here in our world you can work your ass off your entire life just like the aforementioned commoner, but if you step one foot out of society\u2019s script you\u2019ll face everything from social shunning to jail time. Barriers to your success will materialize like magic to make sure you stay mired in whatever social stratum the bastards in control arbitrarily placed you in. And despite claims of meritocracy, no amount of work will ever make a difference since it\u2019s all about social standing and clout. Yes in D&amp;D there\u2019s things like bandits/brigands/pirates/thieves, but those already exist here in our world and have existed for all of time. Yes D&amp;D worlds have plagues and such, but we just got out of a pandemic without any clerical healing to work with. There\u2019s entitled and self-absorbed nobles and a feudalistic system, but what do you think the billionaires are trying to do with this country now? There\u2019s monsters that can raid smaller settlements and infest cities, but weigh that against hate-groups, psychos, and gestapos running amok.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on which D&amp;D world we're talking about here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Forgotten Realms</b> or <b>Eberron</b>? Maybe... There would be some information I'd need to look into, such as whether or not the <i>Wall of the Faithless</i> still exists.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravenloft</b> or <b>Darksun</b>? Hell NO!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I think you're overlooking one very crucial detail: <i>Established Lore</i>. While you are correct in that mechanically anybody has the potential to better their lives, they narratively are not in the habit of doing so. Adventurers are exceptional individuals among their kind, not a standard norm. Then there's the canonically established racism.<br /> <br /> <br /> Gods help you if you're reincarnated as a <i>Tiefling</i>, because you're NOT going to be the sexual icon that modern players think they are. What's actually going to happen, is you are abandoned at birth; and assuming you don't die in infancy, you're going to go through life being seen as a vile hellspawn that is here to steal our souls.<br /> <br /> Even the <i>Drow</i> themselves have little knowledge about <i>Eilistraee's</i> existence, due to the machinations of <i>Lolth's</i> followers. Which means the surface folk would have virtually none at all. Imagine you spent weeks trying to flee from the Underdark, and when you finally make it to the surface and see the light of day, some 'hero' with a crossbow shoots you in the face without so much as a word.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for level progression, most adventurers tend to retire from the profession around level 10-12. This is the point in your career where you get access to your own headquarters, such as a castle, wizard tower, thieves guild, temple, est. You start attracting apprentices who wish to learn from you. The people who stick around long enough to reach level 14+, are the people who are on the path to becoming demigods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-09-2026, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T01:59:53-08:00","id":1557583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice?p=1557382#post1557382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for level progression, most adventurers tend to retire from the profession around level 10-12. This is the point in your career where you get access to your own headquarters, such as a castle, wizard tower, thieves guild, temple, est. You start attracting apprentices who wish to learn from you. The people who stick around long enough to reach level 14+, are the people who are on the path to becoming demigods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's even that high.<br /> <br /> First, when the game even has rules for establishing headquarters and attracting apprentices, it's around level 5 or 6. It was 10th level only for AD&amp;D 2nd Ed, neither before or after.<br /> <br /> Also I don't think it should be taken as granted that most adventurers either live to that point or retire only when they have their own guild. In my games most actually retire as adventurers by level 3 or slightly above, simply because at this point they already solved whatever caused their adventuring to begin with, and now have the means to establish themselves into a more mundane job with enough perks to live with some comfort, which isn't very ambitious, but is far better than living miserably in the wilds looking for new ways to put your life in danger.<br /> <br /> Not to say that even those who live as &quot;adventurers&quot; won't necessarily see or seek the almost linear growth of challenge we see on regular campaigns. No rule says you can't end up facing things way above your weight category by pure accident, and the story behind most adventures make it very clear that this is exactly what happened to a lot of people before the PCs arrive. At the same time, though, a mercenary or other &quot;adventurer&quot; type isn't at all guaranteed or required to face threats at their level, and after reaching level 3 or above they may very well settle for dealing with minor problems (that tend to be also very common) for the rest of their lives (which means an ever slowing increase in level if we assume all rules are followed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T14:59:00-08:00","id":1557714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice?p=1557583#post1557583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's even that high.<br /> <br /> First, when the game even has rules for establishing headquarters and attracting apprentices, it's around level 5 or 6. It was 10th level only for AD&amp;D 2nd Ed, neither before or after.<br /> <br /> Also I don't think it should be taken as granted that most adventurers either live to that point or retire only when they have their own guild. In my games most actually retire as adventurers by level 3 or slightly above, simply because at this point they already solved whatever caused their adventuring to begin with, and now have the means to establish themselves into a more mundane job with enough perks to live with some comfort, which isn't very ambitious, but is far better than living miserably in the wilds looking for new ways to put your life in danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, something to keep in mind is the fact that you receiving your headquarters assumes you are the highest ranking official within said headquarters.<br /> <br /> Meaning that your subordinates would likely be lower level than you. So if you're retiring from the active field at around level 5 or so, then the people serving under you would be somewhere around levels 1-3, depending on their level of seniority.<br /> <br /> Which would explain why the people don't treat death as a minor inconvenience by dragging all their loved ones off to the nearest temple to get raised. It's because that level of magic is actually much rarer to come by than the player base would have you believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T14:27:48-07:00","id":1562350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice?p=1557583#post1557583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also I don't think it should be taken as granted that most adventurers either live to that point or retire only when they have their own guild. In my games most actually retire as adventurers by level 3 or slightly above, simply because at this point they already solved whatever caused their adventuring to begin with, and now have the means to establish themselves into a more mundane job with enough perks to live with some comfort, which isn't very ambitious, but is far better than living miserably in the wilds looking for new ways to put your life in danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you realize that the annual salary for most peasants is a mere 2 silver pieces, you get a new perspective on finding a chest that has 'only' 10 gold pieces in it.<br /> <br /> Those 10 GP could sustain a family for decades.<br /> <br /> If your coin purse has hundreds, or even thousands of GP, you pretty much never have to work again, because you can afford anything a commoner might need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-20T06:08:40-07:00","id":1564866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice?p=1557382#post1557382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gods help you if you're reincarnated as a <i>Tiefling</i>, because you're NOT going to be the sexual icon that modern players think they are. What's actually going to happen, is you are abandoned at birth; and assuming you don't die in infancy, you're going to go through life being seen as a vile hellspawn that is here to steal our souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is just ridiculous! Hell does not steal souls, <i>it buys them!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice?p=1557382#post1557382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even the <i>Drow</i> themselves have little knowledge about <i>Eilistraee's</i> existence, due to the machinations of <i>Lolth's</i> followers. Which means the surface folk would have virtually none at all. Imagine you spent weeks trying to flee from the Underdark, and when you finally make it to the surface and see the light of day, some 'hero' with a crossbow shoots you in the face without so much as a word.</div> </div> </div> </div>For those wondering how this is possible, given that she's part of the Dark Seldarine, it should be noted the Drow do not experience Trance the same way surface elves do.<br /> <br /> When a surface elf goes into Trance, they experience memories relating to their past lives, all the way back to the time of their original existence. This allows them to retain a connection to their history throughout the millennia.<br /> <br /> Drow, on the other hand, only experience sensory deprivation. No light, no sound, no memories, just all encompassing darkness. It's not even clear on whether or not they reincarnate like other elves. As such, memories of their past, and of Eilistraee would have gradually vanished over the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-04T10:45:38-08:00","id":1565130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice#post1554478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my case; I absolutely would since ALL D&amp;D worlds, even the really hostile and shitty ones like Dark Sun have a factor this world does not; linear progression. Any commoner who has the simple gumption to do so, can better their lot in life by leaving the quotidian script society applies to their lives and venturing out into the unknown to find their fortune. The instant you start doing this, you start earning EXP (unless your DM is one of those milestone people), and you start seeing measurable improvement in yourself and you life. It sounds ridiculous until you realize that D&amp;D worlds are lousy with buried ruins, lost keeps, monster lairs, and all manner of magicked insanity waiting to be discovered. A simple snatch and grab can set you up for a year, and a large enough score is a total quality of life upgrade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the monster manuals?<br /> <br /> Do you know what kind of shit is lurking in those ruins?<br /> <br /> You probably haven't even heard of the 'Ooze Wall' before, have you? It's an ooze... the size of a wall... and it camouflages itself as one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then there's the Rust Beast, who can damage, or even permanently destroy your weapons and armor by causing them to rapidly degrade.<br /> <br /> <br /> In previous editions of D&amp;D, an encounter with even the most basic forms of Undead were legitimately terrifying, because they had the ability to inflict PERMANENT DRAIN on your ability scores and character levels. If you wanted to cleanse the affliction, you either needed restorative magic, or you had to earn those levels back the hard way.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but some monsters were way harder to defeat than they are now. Vampires and Lycanthropes didn't have this bull shit &quot;resistance&quot; that makes them take only half damage. No, they were were just straight up <b>immune</b> to non-magical weaponry that wasn't silver. Meaning that if you encountered them at low levels, and didn't have an offensive caster around, you were pretty much screwed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-04T11:09:18-08:00","id":1565132,"title":"","content":"I've got horrible emotional problems so i want to be in 3rd ed ravenloft.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j-peDxv2LZI?is=UFQqRtQqh9Nggu8d\" data-code=\"j-peDxv2LZI\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/j-peDxv2LZI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-08T12:56:36-08:00","id":1565184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1554478-would-you-leave-this-world-for-a-d-d-world-if-given-the-choice?p=1565130#post1565130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read the monster manuals?<br /> <br /> Do you know what kind of shit is lurking in those ruins?<br /> <br /> You probably haven't even heard of the 'Ooze Wall' before, have you? It's an ooze... the size of a wall... and it camouflages itself as one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then there's the Rust Beast, who can damage, or even permanently destroy your weapons and armor by causing them to rapidly degrade.<br /> <br /> <br /> In previous editions of D&amp;D, an encounter with even the most basic forms of Undead were legitimately terrifying, because they had the ability to inflict PERMANENT DRAIN on your ability scores and character levels. If you wanted to cleanse the affliction, you either needed restorative magic, or you had to earn those levels back the hard way.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but some monsters were way harder to defeat than they are now. Vampires and Lycanthropes didn't have this bull shit &quot;resistance&quot; that makes them take only half damage. No, they were were just straight up <b>immune</b> to non-magical weaponry that wasn't silver. Meaning that if you encountered them at low levels, and didn't have an offensive caster around, you were pretty much screwed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, but eventually, humans will manage to kill all the monsters, demi-humans and the world will turn into Game of Thrones with some magic and monsters, but mostly human-interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}